%% alt: A ticket or prompt reaches the orchestrator, which applies queues, quotas and policy and starts an ephemeral sandbox per task. Inside the sandbox the agent loop works on a repository worktree, runs build, test and lint in a shell, and uses read-only sub-agents for search and review. Model calls go through the AI gateway; network egress reaches only the package mirror and git server. The agent's output is a branch and pull request, which CI checks with tests, static analysis and secret scanning before human review and approval, then merge. Traces, commands and the network log are kept.
flowchart TB
  T[Ticket or prompt]:::human --> O[Orchestrator<br/>queue, quotas, policy]:::control
  O --> A
  subgraph S[Ephemeral sandbox per task]
    A[Agent loop]:::model --> X[Repo worktree, shell<br/>build, test, lint]:::tool
    A --> R[Read-only sub-agents<br/>search, review]:::model
  end
  A -->|model calls| G[AI gateway]:::control
  X -->|egress allow-list| P[Package mirror,<br/>git server]:::tool
  X --> PR[Branch +<br/>pull request]:::tool --> CI[CI<br/>tests, SAST, secret scan]:::control
  CI --> H[Human review<br/>and approval]:::human --> M[Merge]:::tool
  M ~~~ L[(Traces, commands,<br/>network log)]:::data
  S -.-> L
